<title>USA: Glens Falls, N.Y., turns down city-owned utility.</title>
<headline>Glens Falls, N.Y., turns down city-owned utility.</headline>
<text>
<p>NEW YORK, Nov 6 (Reuter) Voters in Glens Falls, N.Y., overwhelmingly rejected a plan to borrow $38 million to create a city-owned electric company.</p>
<p>The measure failed by a three-to-one-margin, though eight rural northern municipalities voted to get rid of Niagara Mohawk Power Company in favor of locally generated electricity.</p>
<p>Those referendums are non-binding.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
</text>
